  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Saving Endangered Sun Parakeets in Guyana</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) training and supporting the villagers to improve their capacity as parakeet conservationists; (2) studying and monitoring the species population dynamics and reproductive biology as little is known about this species in the wild and this knowledge is needed to protect them; (3) developing sustainable parrot conservation efforts through ecotourism strategies for local communities; (4) supporting education and awareness activities within the village area and on the national level; and (5) growing the capacity and networking of all of the various stakeholders involved in parrot conservation in Guyana by conducting a sun parakeet conservation workshop in Georgetown, developing online networking platforms, and drafting and disseminating a long-term conservation plan.</narrative>
  </description>
